# Design Brief

> **Do NOT invent — fill this by interviewing the team and reading the real codebase.**
> This is the product bible. Every UI decision is checked against it before implementation.
> If a proposed design does not serve the users, voice, and constraints defined here, it is wrong.

---

## Product definition

**What it is:**
<< One sentence: what does this product do and for whom? >>

**What it is NOT:**
<< List 2–4 explicit non-goals. Name the category of problem this product deliberately ignores. >>

**Core value proposition:**
<< Why would a user choose this over the alternative? One sentence. >>

**Primary job the product does:**
<< Complete: "When I [situation], help me [motivation] so I can [outcome]." >>

